From 92af472f0e9dc59baf00e41279e150e5047ff0a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Markus Hoffmann <markus@thehoffs.at>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 18:54:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add per-indicator settings for container tab color and
 terminal footer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Introduces two independent settings under Tab Bar → Appearance:

- ShowContainerTabColor (default: on): color-codes the tab with a
  per-container color when the foreground process is inside a container
  such as Distrobox or Toolbox.
- ShowContainerStatusBar (default: on): shows a label at the bottom of
  the terminal area with the container type and name.

Both settings take effect immediately when toggled; no restart needed.
User-explicitly-set tab colors are never suppressed: when the container
indicator is off its auto-assigned color is skipped rather than
invalidated, so a sibling pane's explicit color survives in a split.

Adds two unit tests to ViewManagerTest covering the suppression of
auto-container colors and the preservation of user-set colors.

Documents the container awareness feature in the handbook.
